  "body": "Takeover: the coordinator session of NeoTech refreshed this PR by the maintainer's order; the author is mkinney.\n\n## State\n\nPR #2149 is on `main`. This branch has merged `main` (`ee91ac3e5`), and `main` is an ancestor of the head `e047966c2`. The PR now changes only its own files:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/entry.rs`\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/floor_levels.rs`\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/mod.rs`\n- `crates/motion/tests/blind_floor.rs`\n- `docs/decisions/2088-shallow-floor-levels.md`\n\nThe PR changes no process file.\n\n## What changed\n\n3D Pocket now cuts a 3 mm blind hole at its floor with a 4 mm stepdown. The level planner adds flat upward floors, plus `stock_to_leave`, inside the first depth interval. The added levels obey the same material, entry, shell, mask and protected-area checks as the regular levels. The planner refuses excessive floor levels by name.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe regular depth ladder used the levels -4, -8, -12 and -15 for the test hole. It missed the floor at -3. The material checks correctly refused every lower level, because solid material stood above it. The operation then refused with \"nothing to cut\".\n\n## Where the floor levels apply\n\n- The 3D Pocket sites get the discovered floor levels:\n  - plain and offset-shell (`run_plain_with`, with the open-side and avoid variants);\n  - the coarse and rest legs (`run_rest_with`);\n  - trochoidal (`pocket3d_trochoidal`, through the two functions above);\n  - the multi-axis rough, which follows the path of `pocket3d`.\n- The rotary air-split ladder (`pocket3d_air_split`, called only by the rotary wrap) keeps the plain level law (commit `7caff3125`). In the wrap, a flat face is the turned skin of the bar, not a blind floor. A height window whose only open level is the wrap top is air and must be refused. Without this split, `rotary_offset::the_height_window_names_the_stations_and_refuses_an_empty_one` got a toolpath in an air window.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe six tests of `crates/motion/tests/blind_floor.rs`:\n\n- `a_blind_hole_shallower_than_one_stepdown_is_cut_at_its_floor`: the 3 mm hole at stepdown 4 is cut at one level, Z -3, for `pocket3d` and `pocket3d_offset`. No gouge, and the verify is silent.\n- `a_shallow_floor_keeps_stock_allowance_and_the_top_stock_level`: with `stock_to_leave` 0.5 the level is at -2.5 and no move is below it. With stock over Top Z, the Top Z stock level stays.\n- `excessive_shallow_floor_levels_are_refused_by_name`: `MAX_PASSES` added flat heights give the named refusal.\n- `the_rotary_air_split_ladder_keeps_the_plain_level_law`: on the same hole, `pocket3d` cuts and `pocket3d_air_split` refuses with `GenError::Empty`.\n- `a_blind_pocket_never_enters_solid_under_any_ladder`: the matrix keeps its no-gouge, no-move-under-the-floor and silent-verify asserts. It now cuts all 1152 cases. The 64 removed \"nothing to cut\" refusals were the cases with hole depth 3 mm, stepdown 4 mm and Bottom Z under the hole: an open blind hole that must be cut.\n- `the_islands_law_shadows_a_blind_floor_all_the_way_down`: the existing islands-law test. It did not change.\n\nMutation checks (each one reverted after the run):\n\n- All floor-level calls back to `cut_levels_under`: 5 of 6 `blind_floor` tests fail.\n- `+ p.stock_to_leave` removed in `floor_levels.rs`: `a_shallow_floor_keeps_stock_allowance_and_the_top_stock_level` fails.\n- `pocket3d_air_split` back to the floor levels: the rotary pin fails, and `rotary_offset.rs:328` fails.\n\n## Gates (Windows x86_64, head `e047966c2`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=18`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 38 steps, 0 failed.\n- Rotary and multi-axis suites, debug, 0 failed:\n  - motion: `multiaxis`, `multiaxis_avoid`, `multiaxis_rough`, `rotary`, `rotary_adaptive`, `rotary_dflat`, `rotary_links`, `rotary_offset`, `avoid_pocket`.\n  - app: `blind_floor`, `center_cut_multiaxis`, `mcp_rotary_stack`, `rotary_face_selection`, `rotary_feed_cap`, `rotary_field_parity`, `rotary_letter`, `rotary_subplate`, `rotary_subplate_standing`, `rotary_verify`, `setup_align_multiaxis`.\n  - sim: `verify_avoid`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 2 steps, 0 failed.\n- Selected heavy steps: 17 of 18 pass. They include `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`, the pocket3d steps and the rotary and multi-axis steps.\n- The red heavy step is `app pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. It fails with the same triple `(3158, 3130, 1141)` on unmodified `main` `ee91ac3e5`. This PR adds no level there (Z 15, 10, 5, 0). Refs #3050\n\nNo golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe other heavy steps that the diff reaches, the release gate and physical machining were not run. Floor discovery covers only exactly flat upward faces in the first depth interval.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Cut shallow flat blind floors in 3D Pocket when the stepdown exceeds the hole depth.\nFixes #2088\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
